   "short_name": "Weather",
   "long_name": "NASA Weather and Atmospheric Dynamics Focus Area",
   "notes_public": "The Earth's weather system includes the dynamics of the atmosphere and its interaction with the oceans and land. The scale ranges from local or microphysical processes that occur in minutes through global-scale phenomena that can be predicted with a degree of success at an estimated maximum of two weeks prior.",
